steps.text:
Playwright lets Claude open your site in a real browser, screenshot it and self-QA. Install it with:

``` Command: Add Playwright MCP
claude mcp add playwright --scope user -- npx -y
@playwright/mcp@latest
```

Or add it to your ~/.claude.json (or a per-project .mcp.json):

``` Config: Playwright in .mcp.json
{
"mcpServers": {
"playwright": {
"command": "npx",
"args": ["-y", "@playwright/mcp@latest"]
}
}
}
```

Restart Claude Code. The first run downloads the Chromium binary (about 200MB, one time). Run /mcp and you should see playwright in the connected list. Test with:

``` Prompt: Screenshot and check a page
Open my dev server at localhost:3000, screenshot it, and tell me if the hero section looks broken.
```
